# Onec Query Strategy

This is optional guidance for the main onec-context skill. Load
[the reference](reference.md) when this topic is relevant. Executable tools live
in the main skill or an exported bundle, not in this supplemental directory.
Resolve their actual location before running a command. Do not assume that
`onec-context` is installed on PATH.

Choose the layer that can prove the claim:

| Question | Role | Reader |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Platform syntax or built-in API | `platform` | `local_kb_query.py` |
| ITS development convention | `standards` | `local_kb_query.py` |
| Object, field, type, form or command | `metadata` | `local_kb_query.py` |
| Module, declaration or call relationship | `code` | `query_code_pack.py` |
| Exact source file contents | `full` | `query_config_pack.py` |

The installed toolkit provides `scripts/onec_context.py resolve-packs
--workspace-root /path/to/project`. An exported read-only bundle instead provides
`tools/resolve_packs.py --bundle-dir /path/to/bundle`. Resolve script paths from
the toolkit or bundle root, not from the project being examined. Both readers
accept `--role`, `--target` and `--path-only`. Inspect available targets first.
Do not assume pack filenames or select the first configuration implicitly.

For platform, metadata and standards, use `tools/local_kb_query.py --db
/path/to/resolved-pack --q "name" --exact --json`. Drop `--exact` for lexical
FTS5 search. Use `--version` for a platform claim and `--detail full` for a
preserved record. Separate examples use `--domain api_examples`.

The installed toolkit can prepare missing layers using `ensure`. The exported
bundle cannot build them: report what is missing and request preparation with
the toolkit. Do not run a rebuild before every lookup. After configuration source
edits, explicitly rebuild the affected profile; status does not hash every file.

A full record is the extractor's saved record, not the original HTML or a
cross-layer answer. No match means unconfirmed in this pack. Keep source facts,
code deductions and unresolved assumptions distinguishable.
